            <offset unit="byte">113</offset>
            <records>1382400</records>
            <description>This table contains brightness temperatures and bolometric
                brightness temperatures from the Diviner Lunar Radiometer Experiment
                binned at 0.5 degree latitude and longitude and 0.25 hours of local
                time derived from a compilation of all nadir observations acquired
                from 5-July-2009 to 1-April-2015. Negative brightness temperatures
                result from negative radiance values obtained by a sensor when
                temperatures are below the sensitivity of a Diviner channel.
                Constant -9999 corresponds to bins that contained no observations.
                For more information, see: Williams et al. (2017)
                </description>
